# This repository is LF, everywhere, in the object store and in the checkout.
#
# `git ls-files --eol` reported **zero** committed files with CRLF when this
# rule was written (2026-08-06), so it renormalises nothing — it records what
# is already true and stops the two ways a Windows host quietly breaks it.
#
# Both ways have cost this project real time:
#
# 1. **Smudged checkouts break source-level guards.** Several tests in this tree
#    `include_str!` their own file and assert on its text, because the property
#    is about what the code *contains* and only the text can see it (`LE-99`'s
#    stamp-density guard, `hal_arm64::ethernet`'s cadence guard,
#    `kernel::measure_phases`' G23 pair equivalence). Those needles are
#    whitespace-pinned, so a checkout that turns LF into CRLF fails them for a
#    reason that has nothing to do with the property. It is not hypothetical and
#    it is not rare: it fires in exactly the workflow `CONCURRENT_SESSIONS`
#    rule 8 *mandates*. A `git worktree add` on a host with
#    `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF, so the session verifying its own subset
#    over clean `HEAD` — the prescribed way to work around another session's
#    broken row — sees `board_dispatch`'s guard red on code it never touched,
#    with no way to tell that from a real break (`LE-101`).
#
# 2. **Smudged *writes* land as diff noise.** An editor that rewrites a file
#    with CRLF turns a one-line amendment into a whole-file rewrite: on
#    2026-08-06 a single amended paragraph in `SeedMVP.md` staged as 1,270
#    changed lines, and one added row in `EPIC-P1.md` as 125. That is history
#    and blame destroyed for every line of both documents, in a commit about
#    something else, and staging alone does not clean it — this attribute does.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text (binaries are untouched); `eol=lf`
# fixes the checkout, which is the half `core.autocrlf` gets wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden transcripts are byte-exact evidence (TEST-P2-07-01-A) and opt out of
# all of the above: no conversion in either direction, ever. A Windows checkout
# must see the same bytes CI's Linux checkout sees, or the host golden test reds
# on a fake divergence (found 2026-07-30 while executing hand-2026-07-30/04A).
# Last, so this rule wins over the blanket one above.
*.golden.txt -text
